2026-06-01 14:56:26,283 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: ### Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., leading a consortium with expertise in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT, proposes an intelligent assistance tool for municipal agents of the City of Belval. This solution leverages Large Language Models (LLMs) like Mistral 7B Instruct, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities, and integrates with existing systems via REST, GraphQL, or SOAP APIs, ensuring compliance with GDPR regulations, data sovereignty, and environmental sustainability.

### Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires an AI-powered assistance solution to improve the efficiency of administrative services. The proposed system must facilitate access to information, enhance answer quality, reduce processing times, and comply with regulatory requirements such as GDPR. Additionally, it should ensure data sovereignty by hosting on EU territory, achieve high availability (99.9%), integrate with existing software via APIs, and minimize environmental footprint.

### Proposed Solution
Our consortium proposes a hybrid cloud deployment using SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure, integrating containerized microservices for API integration with civil status software, town planning software, electronic document management (EDM), and user directories. We utilize OVHcloud and Scaleway, both offering 100% renewable energy and having Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) scores of 1.3 and 1.28, respectively.

For the AI component, we employ Mistral 7B Instruct, a sovereign model that can be fine-tuned to adapt to the municipal agents' domain-specific tone and format. Our RAG capabilities include dense vector semantic search and BM25 sparse retrieval strategies for quick access to reliable information. Explainability methods such as source citation, chain-of-thought display, and confidence scoring ensure transparency in AI recommendations.

To meet security requirements, we implement data encryption (anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio), ensure no automated decision-making without explicit agent validation, and conduct regular penetration testing with partners like Synacktiv and HN Security. Our risk management includes maintaining a risk register reviewed bi-weekly.

Compliance-wise, our default IP model is work-for-hire, ensuring all deliverables are transferred to the client upon final payment. We have standard contractual clauses in place for GDPR compliance and adhere to Article 6(1)(e) as the legal basis for processing personal data.

Budget-wise, with a maximum contract value eligibility of €3 million, we target a gross margin of 28% but can adjust to meet the client's cost optimization needs without sacrificing quality. Assuming an 18% minimum acceptable margin, our projected margin over the 4-year contract duration would be approximately €540,000.

For sustainability, by partnering with OVHcloud and Scaleway, both using 100% renewable energy, and implementing digital sobriety practices like INT8/INT4 model quantization (reducing GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%) and auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, we contribute to reducing energetic consumption. Our equipment has a minimum lifecycle of 5 years, further supporting sustainability.

### Unaddressed Requirements
Given the strict adherence to provided information, there are no explicitly mentioned requirements from the tender that our proposal does not address based on the agents' contributions.

### Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l.'s consortium offers a comprehensive solution that addresses the City of Belval's needs for an AI-powered assistance tool. By leveraging specific technologies like Mistral 7B Instruct, integrating with existing systems through APIs, ensuring GDPR compliance and data sovereignty, and focusing on sustainability, we are confident in our ability to deliver a high-quality solution within the specified budget and timeline. Our approach not only meets but exceeds the client's expectations by incorporating explainability, transparency, and environmental considerations, making us an ideal partner for this project.
